      "summaries": {
        "en": "LightX2V is an open-source framework that simplifies video generation by making complex diffusion models more accessible and efficient for developers. It employs an auto-regressive diffusion approach that breaks down video creation into manageable sequential steps, reducing computational demands while maintaining quality. Developers can use it to prototype creative video applications, experiment with conditional generation, or integrate it into pipelines for generating short clips from text or image prompts, enabling practical exploration of AI-driven video synthesis.",
        "zh": "LightX2V是一个轻量级视频生成推理框架，旨在降低扩散模型在视频创作中的应用门槛，让开发者能更便捷地实现高质量视频合成。它采用自回归扩散技术，将视频生成分解为序列化步骤，在保持视觉连贯性的同时优化计算效率。用户可通过该框架快速搭建文本到视频或图像到视频的生成原型，尝试条件控制生成效果，或将其集成到多媒体处理流程中，为创意表达和动态内容生成提供灵活的实验平台。",
        "es": "LightX2V is an open-source framework that simplifies video generation by making complex diffusion models more accessible and efficient for developers. It employs an auto-regressive diffusion approach that breaks down video creation into manageable sequential steps, reducing computational demands while maintaining quality. Developers can use it to prototype creative video applications, experiment with conditional generation, or integrate it into pipelines for generating short clips from text or image prompts, enabling practical exploration of AI-driven video synthesis.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "LightX2V stands out for auto-regressive-diffusion-model, diffusion-models, and video-generation in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "LightX2V is an open-source framework that simplifies video generation by making complex diffusion models more accessible and efficient for developers. It employs an auto-regressive diffusion approach that breaks down video creation into manageable sequential steps, reducing computational demands while maintaining quality. Developers can use it to prototype creative video applications, experiment with conditional generation, or integrate it into pipelines for generating short clips from text or image prompts, enabling practical exploration of AI-driven video synthesis.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ModelTC/LightX2V for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
